  "notes": "University Park. The 'BIOL 444 or GEOSC 472A' item lists BIOL 444 first per the bulletin's own order, but BIOL 444 needs BIOL 220W (not otherwise part of this plan) — relies on the engine's option-fallback fix to resolve to GEOSC 472A instead, whose own requirement (concurrent with GEOSC 310) is satisfied. 'Supporting Course' pool (17-18 credits, bulletin: 'supportive of the student's interest') is modeled generically. Real prereq-fix fallout, two separate issues: (1) BIOL 234 and BIOL 235W now have a genuinely circular prereq pair in the catalog (234 requires 235W-or-236W, 235W requires 234 back) -- an unsatisfiable deadlock, almost certainly a lecture/lab concurrent-registration pair the scraper mis-captured as sequential prereqs instead of concurrent. Replaced both with BIOL 230W (Biology: Molecules and Cells, 4cr, prereq only BIOL 110 which is already scheduled) -- the catalog's own BIOL 236W entry explicitly notes students who passed BIOL 230W may not enroll in 236W, confirming they cover the same requirement; nothing else in this plan needs literal BIOL 234. (2) CHEM 110 now requires MATH 22, which itself requires MATH 21, MATH 4, and MATH 3 in turn -- a full remedial placement chain never otherwise scheduled in this plan -- added all four as explicit early-semester items; the engine's own scheduler pushes CHEM 110 (and its downstream 111/112/113) out to whichever later term MATH 22 actually completes in, and the whole plan still finishes in 8 terms at this major's existing 17cr/semester cap. Handbook-verification pass (2026-08-26): the bulletin's own 'Requirements for the Major' text (bulletins.psu.edu's programrequirementstext.pdf) specifies the 12-credit 'Advanced GEOBI elective' pool must come 'at least 3 credits from each' of two named categories -- evolution/paleobiology/geology, and biogeochemistry -- and a real department curriculum sheet (Penn State Geosciences, hosted at serc.carleton.edu/download/files/8199/penn_state_geobio.pdf) names the two categories' course lists. Wired via a match regex combining both lists, using only the codes still present in this app's own scraped GEOSC/BIOL/ANTH/SOILS catalogs (GEOSC 425 and GEOSC 412 from that sheet no longer exist in the current catalog -- likely retired/renumbered since the sheet was published -- and GEOSC 413 is now cataloged as GEOSC 413W; all three excluded/updated rather than guessed at). The 'at least 3 credits from each category' sub-minimum isn't separately enforced -- a single match slot can't express a cross-category minimum -- same category of documented limitation as CMPSC's own Department List Elective exclusions.",
